CREATED:20260810T140030Z
DESCRIPTION:The High Holidays are right around the corner\, and Jewish Lif
 e at Duke is excited to welcome you to the Freeman Center to observe them
 . All are welcome to holiday services and meals.\n\nDuke students are inv
 ited to enjoy free\, kosher High Holiday meals at the Freeman Center for 
 Jewish Life\; registration is required here by Wednesday\, September 9 at
  5:00pm: duke.is/HighHolidays\n\nFriday\, September 11\, 2026\nErev Rosh 
 Hashanah\n\n6:30pm: Erev Rosh Hashanah Community Service \n7:30pm: Erev R
 osh Hashanah Holiday Dinner (Free for students\; registration required by
  September 9)\n\nSaturday\, September 12\, 2026  \nFirst Day of Rosh Hash
 anah\n\n9:30am: Conservative Service\n10:00am: Reform Service\n10:45am (a
 pprox.): Communal Torah Reading\n12:00pm (approx.): Musaf \nFollowing Ser
 vices ~1:00pm: Rosh Hashanah Kiddush Lunch (Free for students\; registrat
 ion required by September 9)\n6:30pm: Holiday Dinner (Free for students\;
  registration required by September 9)\n7:30pm: Conservative Service and 
 Kiddush \n\nSunday\, September 13\, 2026\nSecond Day of Rosh Hashanah\n\n
 9:30am: Conservative Service\n1:30 - 2:30pm: Tashlikh Service followed by
  Holiday Picnic Lunch at Duke Gardens (meet at the Big Pond\, lunch at th
 e amphitheater by the Big Pond) (Free for students\; registration require
 d by September 9)
DURATION:P2D
