 olle
CREATED:20260909T201450Z
DESCRIPTION:Microbial aggregates\, called biofilms\, are all around us\,\n
 impacting industry\, agriculture\, and human health in both\nbeneficial a
 nd detrimental ways. Bacteria form biofilms to\nprotect themselves agains
 t a variety of stresses\, and biofilm\nbacteria are significantly more to
 lerant to stressors\, such as\nantibiotics. A key feature that contribute
 s to biofilm resilience is\nthe transcriptional heterogeneity of the biof
 ilm cells. In this talk\,\nI will discuss the methods we are developing t
 o interrogate\nbiofilm physiology\, using Pseudomonas aeruginosa as our m
 odel\nbiofilm organism. Specifically\, I will hit on our recent work\ndev
 eloping a probe-based\, single-cell RNA-sequencing method\nto study spati
 al heterogeneity in biofilms. Overall\, better\nunderstanding of the biof
 ilm at a molecular level will aid in the\ndevelopment of technologies tha
 t will allow for the manipulation\nof biofilms to benefit humanity.
DURATION:PT1H
DTSTAMP:20260909T201450Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260914T120000
LAST-MODIFIED:20260909T201450Z
