CREATED:20260813T180954Z
DESCRIPTION:note: translation during the post-talk Q&A (English-Chinese) w
 ill be facilitated by Karen Shi\, an MA student in East Asian Studies.\n\
 nA different history of Tibet\, revealed through music and ritual.\n\nThi
 s lecture draws on long-term fieldwork in Tibetan regions of China and fo
 cuses on a Catholic community that has sustained a distinctive musical an
 d ritual tradition for over a century.  Rather than treating Tibet as a s
 ingle religious landscape\, the lecture approaches it through sound and r
 itual\, bringing into view historical layers that are not fully captured 
 in written sources.\n\nAt the center is a rare music manuscript over one 
 hundred years old\, written in French\, Latin\, and Tibetan and notated i
 n four-line staff notation. Discovered during fieldwork\, it provides dir
 ect evidence of how Catholic chant entered a Tibetan context and was inco
 rporated into local ritual life.\n\nBy bringing together field observatio
 n and historical materials\, the lecture considers how such evidence resh
 apes existing narratives and reveals a more complex picture of religion a
 nd culture in Tibetan regions of China.\n\nAbout the speaker:\nChenhui Su
 n (孙晨荟) is a musicologist and performer\, a professor at the Institute of
  Music in the Chinese National Academy of Arts\, and a 2026 visiting scho
 lar at the Duke Divinity School.\n\nHer research focuses on Chinese Chris
 tian music\, Chinese traditional music\, and Sino-Western musical exchang
 e\, bringing together fieldwork\, archival research\, and musical practic
 e. She is the author of several award-winning monographs\, held in over t
 wo hundred libraries worldwide\, and a contributor to "The Oxford Handboo
 k of the Bible in China\," with a chapter on Chinese church music.\n\nShe
  has conceived and participated in the large-scale concert Sacred Music i
 n China since the Tang Dynasty\, and has taught courses such as "History 
 of Christian Music" and "Chinese Christian Music" at universities and sem
 inaries in China and abroad.\n\nAbstract and speaker information in Chine
 se:\n本讲座基于作者在中国藏区开展的长期田野调查，聚焦一个延续逾百年的藏族天主教社区及其音乐与礼仪传统。讲座不将藏地视为单一宗教空间，而是以声
 音与礼仪为线索，呈现那些未被文本充分记录的历史层次。\n\n田野中发现的一份百年音乐手稿，以法文、拉丁文与藏文并置书写，并采用四线谱记录，为天主教
 圣咏进入藏地并在当地礼仪中被实践提供了直接证据。通过结合田野观察与历史文献，讲座将讨论：这些具体材料如何构成对既有历史叙述的补充与修正，并呈现一个
 更为复杂的藏地宗教与文化图景。\n\n音乐学者、演奏家，现任中国艺术研究院音乐研究所教授，杜克大学神学院访问学者。 研究方向为中国基督教音乐、中国
 传统音乐及中西音乐交流，结合田野调查、文献研究与音乐实践展开相关工作。出版多部获奖学术专著，被全球二百余所图书馆收藏，并为学术权威著作 The O
 xford Handbook of the Bible in China 撰写"中国教会音乐"相关章节。曾策划并参与"唐代以来的中国圣乐"大型学术
 音乐会，长期在国内外高校及神学院讲授《基督宗教音乐史》、《中国基督教音乐》等课程。
DURATION:PT1H30M
