DESCRIPTION:<b>REGISTRATION</b>: <a href="https://duke.is/g/pa4w" target="
 _blank">Click Here</a>\n\n<i>NOTE: We have reached the zoom room capacity
  for this event. Please complete the wait list survey\, and you will be s
 ent the meeting information if capacity opens up. </i>\n\nJoin us for the
  Duke Office of Scientific Integrity's Research Town Hall " Authorship in
  Academic Research: Navigating Integrity\, Policy\, and Practice " on Sep
 tember 15th from 12:00pm - 1:30pm. \n\nAuthorship is one of the most fund
 amental elements of academic research. Our expert panel of speakers will 
 explore authorship from multiple angles\, including Duke's new <a href="h
 ttps://policies.provost.duke.edu/docs/research-integrity#32-authorship" t
 arget="_blank">authorship policy</a>\, authorship rights\, generative AI 
 and authorship\, and considerations in   international collaborations.  T
 he town hall will end with a panel discussion that will take questions pr
 e-submitted through the registration link and submitted live during the e
 vent.\n\nThis event is only open to current Duke faculty\, staff\, and st
 udents. Attending this event fulfills the <b>RCR-200</b> requirement for 
 Faculty and Staff and the <b>714</b> RCR credit for graduate students. Pa
 rticipants must attend for at least 60 minutes to receive credit.
DURATION:PT1H30M
DTSTAMP:20260803T170100Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260915T120000
LAST-MODIFIED:20260803T170100Z
